WEBVTT

00:00.650 --> 00:03.980
This pic's from when we went to the zoo.

00:04.270 --> 00:07.870
We went to celebrate my recovery 
from my ankle sprain.

00:08.600 --> 00:12.490
Man, Kyouya-san's <i>such</i> a hunk!

00:12.650 --> 00:15.990
Are you two going out already?

00:13.990 --> 00:15.990
Hmm? Uh...

00:15.990 --> 00:20.220
I don't know. He hasn't asked me 
to be his girlfriend or anything.

00:20.220 --> 00:24.000
I've heard that older men tend not to do that.

00:24.360 --> 00:28.440
What did Itsuomi-san say to you 
when he asked you out?

00:29.960 --> 00:35.130
I want you, Yuki.

00:34.210 --> 00:35.130
Whoa.

00:35.790 --> 00:37.390
Don't ask about that.

00:37.910 --> 00:40.260
It's for the couple to know, and nobody else.

00:40.830 --> 00:43.520
Oh, sorry, did I startle you?

00:44.210 --> 00:45.630
<i>Itsuomi-san.</i>

00:49.530 --> 00:50.290
What's up?

02:18.240 --> 02:21.990
Promise

02:21.990 --> 02:24.120
<b>Crêpes</b>

02:22.750 --> 02:24.120
Wow.

02:24.510 --> 02:25.680
Looking good together.

02:25.680 --> 02:27.560
You think so?

02:27.560 --> 02:31.260
I'm glad Kyouya's finally 
taking this stuff seriously.

02:31.260 --> 02:32.630
What stuff?

02:33.100 --> 02:33.880
His love life?

02:33.880 --> 02:36.880
Squee! Stop that, Itsuomi-san!

02:36.880 --> 02:39.270
Oh, I gotta go.

02:39.620 --> 02:41.140
See you two later.

02:42.920 --> 02:46.600
<i>Rin-chan's giving us space, huh?</i>

02:49.560 --> 02:52.020
What are your plans for today?

02:52.900 --> 02:57.530
I have the interview for the part-time
job after 4th period. The café owner,
Madoka-chan's aunt, will conduct it.

02:54.900 --> 02:57.140
Ooh, about time.

02:58.370 --> 03:04.760
<i>The moment we started dating is still fresh 
in my mind, so now I'm all self-conscious.</i>

03:07.400 --> 03:08.700
You look nervous.

03:09.170 --> 03:12.720
It's not a formal interview, right? 
Just saying hello?

03:12.720 --> 03:16.300
<i>Right now, I'm nervous because of you!</i>

03:17.420 --> 03:18.800
<b></b>Itsuomi-san,

03:17.420 --> 03:18.800
<b></b>Itsuomi-san,

03:19.840 --> 03:22.550
<b></b>do you ever get nervous?

03:19.840 --> 03:22.550
<b></b>do you ever get nervous?

03:22.910 --> 03:24.050
Uh...

03:25.660 --> 03:26.590
I guess?

03:26.590 --> 03:27.790
<i>So he doesn't.</i>

03:28.280 --> 03:31.480
Oh, but I have freaked out before.

03:32.040 --> 03:38.440
This big cruise ship I was on was swinging 
from end-to-end like a pendulum.

03:39.800 --> 03:41.320
It nearly got wrecked.

03:42.360 --> 03:44.740
<b></b>I'm glad you survived...

03:42.360 --> 03:44.740
I'm glad you survived...

03:44.360 --> 03:45.200
Me too.

03:50.200 --> 03:51.050
Yuki.

03:52.010 --> 03:53.000
Hold out your hands.

04:00.370 --> 04:03.380
Ich drücke dir die Daumen.

04:04.510 --> 04:09.350
It's a gesture used in Germany
to reassure or encourage someone.

04:04.680 --> 04:09.350
The café owner, Madoka-chan's
aunt, will conduct it.

04:06.230 --> 04:09.350
<i>In Germany? Wow.</i>

04:09.470 --> 04:15.730
What does it mean?

04:10.140 --> 04:12.910
<i>What does it mean?</i>

04:12.480 --> 04:15.730
"I'll keep my fingers crossed for you."

04:12.910 --> 04:15.730
"I'll keep my fingers crossed for you."

04:16.060 --> 04:19.080
<i>Wow, so it's like a good-luck charm.</i>

04:23.220 --> 04:24.090
Good luck.

04:26.280 --> 04:27.650
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

04:28.620 --> 04:31.180
<i>I can tell so much from just that.</i>

04:32.600 --> 04:35.600
<i>It feels like he's giving me this big old hug.</i>

04:35.600 --> 04:37.380
<i>I'm feeling all warm and fuzzy inside...?!</i>

04:37.380 --> 04:38.320
<i>I'm feeling all warm and fuzzy inside...?!</i>

04:42.530 --> 04:45.650
So what if people see us? I don't mind.

04:45.650 --> 04:47.650
<i>I certainly do!</i>

04:48.670 --> 04:51.180
Oh, it's almost time for third period.

04:51.640 --> 04:53.310
I should get going.

04:56.230 --> 04:58.690
I like this hairstyle, too.

05:00.070 --> 05:00.850
<i>E...</i>

05:01.530 --> 05:03.410
<i>Every time.</i>

05:03.690 --> 05:06.220
<i>He keeps dropping these bombs on me.</i>

05:08.930 --> 05:09.700
Hello?

05:09.700 --> 05:11.780
Itsu-kun, it's me.

05:11.780 --> 05:13.730
<i>Oh, Shin, what's up?</i>

05:14.330 --> 05:18.210
Has Emma gone to see you lately?

05:18.640 --> 05:21.000
Nope. She hasn't contacted me, either.

05:21.500 --> 05:22.760
<i>Oh...</i>

05:23.530 --> 05:27.970
<i>Sorry. I still haven't managed 
to tell her about your girlfriend.</i>

05:28.360 --> 05:31.140
<i>It's okay. I know you're in a tough spot.</i>

05:31.960 --> 05:33.400
I'll see her this weekend.

05:34.120 --> 05:36.590
And this time, I'll tell her.

05:37.400 --> 05:40.290
<i>Got it. Let me know.</i>

05:40.290 --> 05:41.050
Sure.

05:42.950 --> 05:44.230
<i>Urk.</i>

05:44.740 --> 05:47.410
<i>I'm starting to get worried 
about the interview.</i>

05:48.370 --> 05:51.770
<i>Ich drücke dir die Daumen!</i>

05:51.770 --> 05:53.500
<i>Okay, I'm good.</i>

05:54.380 --> 05:56.260
<i>Café Grand Blue...</i>

05:56.120 --> 06:00.380
<b>Yummy Coffee and Snacks</b>

05:56.260 --> 05:58.130
<i>It should be around here.</i>

06:00.380 --> 06:03.170
<i>She's standing tall outside...</i>

06:03.700 --> 06:06.490
<i>Is she Madoka-chan's aunt?</i>

06:07.190 --> 06:09.170
Oh, Yuki-chan?

06:12.120 --> 06:14.690
That should do it for the interview.

06:14.690 --> 06:16.270
Thank you for your time.

06:16.610 --> 06:17.890
With that out of the way,

06:19.470 --> 06:22.020
I look forward to working with you, Yuki-chan.

06:22.470 --> 06:26.100
It really sounds like you'll be a great help.

06:26.100 --> 06:28.140
It's usually pretty chill on weekdays,

06:28.140 --> 06:31.530
but things get busy on weekends, so good luck.

06:31.980 --> 06:34.740
We all turn into working robots.

06:36.930 --> 06:38.410
That's the spirit!

06:38.860 --> 06:41.540
Let's do our best together!

06:41.540 --> 06:45.370
<i>Oh, Madoka-chan has this side to her too.</i>

06:45.670 --> 06:47.670
<b>Yummy Coffee and Snacks</b>

06:47.980 --> 06:50.820
I'm happy I got to see you today.

06:51.630 --> 06:56.930
I've wanted to meet Madoka's 
friends for the longest time.

06:57.390 --> 07:01.100
The cheer came back to her when she 
started going to the school for the deaf.

07:01.540 --> 07:06.820
So I've been wanting to repay the people 
in her social circle in some way.

07:07.190 --> 07:12.820
Madoka-chan was
the life of our party.

07:10.030 --> 07:12.510
You mean she's just a walking ruckus.

07:13.480 --> 07:15.700
Take care on your way back!

07:22.140 --> 07:24.660
<i>I finally found a job!</i>

07:25.580 --> 07:31.090
<i>Oh, I should tell Itsuomi-san. 
I hope it makes him happy.</i>

07:31.680 --> 07:33.720
I landed the job!

07:32.590 --> 07:33.720
<b>Yaaay</b>

07:37.970 --> 07:40.980
Buy some okonomiyaki sauce
on your way home, please

07:38.900 --> 07:40.100
<i>Mom.</i>

07:43.720 --> 07:45.180
<i>Let's see...</i>

07:45.180 --> 07:48.930
<i>Where's the lady who always gestures for me?</i>

07:46.110 --> 07:49.230
<b>Do you have a
loyalty card?</b>

07:49.900 --> 07:52.110
<i>Found her. I'll line up there.</i>

07:52.360 --> 07:54.990
<b>Okonomiyaki Sauce
Sweet</b>

07:56.390 --> 07:59.470
Ma'am, I'll ring you up at the next register.

08:00.610 --> 08:02.050
<i>That surprised me...</i>

08:02.380 --> 08:04.220
<i>Huh? Over there?</i>

08:08.830 --> 08:09.420
<i>Hmm?</i>

08:09.910 --> 08:11.310
<i>Did his mask just move?</i>

08:15.640 --> 08:17.800
<i>Are you asking if I brought my own bag?</i>

08:21.130 --> 08:22.600
<i>A loyalty card?</i>

08:24.700 --> 08:27.410
Oh, nah, we're good.

08:28.770 --> 08:30.030
<i>Oushi-kun.</i>

08:31.790 --> 08:34.500
He was asking if you collected 
the discount campaign stickers.

08:34.500 --> 08:35.610
<i>Ah...</i>

08:37.670 --> 08:40.040
A mask makes it hard to lip-read, doesn't it?

08:47.070 --> 08:49.140
<i>As thanks. These are great.</i>

08:49.700 --> 08:52.010
Nah... Well, I guess I'll take it.

08:53.390 --> 08:55.470
Even going to the supermarket 
is an ordeal, huh?

08:56.910 --> 08:59.780
<i>Call me, and I'll go with you anytime.</i>

09:01.870 --> 09:03.580
<i>What's going on?</i>

09:03.580 --> 09:05.530
<i>You're being kinda nice.</i>

09:13.030 --> 09:15.650
I landed the job!

09:13.030 --> 09:15.650
<b>Yaaay</b>

09:13.030 --> 09:15.650
Grats.

09:14.200 --> 09:15.650
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

09:21.400 --> 09:23.580
From whom? That guy?

09:24.990 --> 09:26.290
You two are dating, right?

09:27.410 --> 09:28.960
<i>How do you know that?!</i>

09:29.810 --> 09:31.470
I went drinking with him.

09:31.470 --> 09:33.760
<i>What the... When did you become friends?!</i>

09:33.760 --> 09:34.840
We didn't!

09:39.260 --> 09:41.100
If he...

09:39.420 --> 09:40.530
<i>If he...</i>

09:41.390 --> 09:43.640
ever

09:41.960 --> 09:43.930
<i>ever makes you cry or hurts you,</i>

09:42.510 --> 09:44.850
makes you cry or hurts you,

09:45.390 --> 09:47.350
tell me

09:45.900 --> 09:47.700
<i>tell me about it.</i>

09:46.890 --> 09:49.270
about it.

09:50.510 --> 09:55.470
<i>I hate him, so I'll deal with him for you.</i>

09:59.190 --> 10:02.270
<i>Did you not realize when you 
went drinking with him?</i>

10:04.340 --> 10:09.000
<i>It's hard for anyone to hate Itsuomi-san.</i>

10:09.710 --> 10:12.040
<i>He's really nice...</i>

10:14.620 --> 10:17.350
Don't praise him.

10:17.860 --> 10:18.510
<i>Huh?</i>

10:19.080 --> 10:23.470
Don't sign that stuff in front of me.

10:32.860 --> 10:34.890
Sorry. Did that hurt?

10:43.590 --> 10:47.810
<i>That was the first time he ever 
stopped me in the middle of signing.</i>

10:48.910 --> 10:54.960
Is something wrong?

10:49.050 --> 10:53.150
<i>I could ask him a bunch of questions 
like, "Is something wrong?",</i>

10:53.150 --> 10:55.650
<i>but I feel like they would all 
miss the mark somewhat.</i>

10:57.820 --> 11:01.380
<i>Oushi-kun really is acting different today.</i>

11:02.670 --> 11:07.250
<i>It's like he's become someone I don't know.</i>

11:10.810 --> 11:12.940
Hurry up!

11:13.630 --> 11:15.010
Shaddup!

11:15.010 --> 11:16.360
Shut up!

11:17.220 --> 11:18.460
Here comes the train!

11:20.090 --> 11:21.580
So loud!

11:21.580 --> 11:23.560
My ears!

11:32.390 --> 11:37.660
<i>We have performed an emergency stop 
due to a malfunction in the train ahead.</i>

11:37.660 --> 11:40.480
<i>We will remain stopped while 
it undergoes a safety check.</i>

11:40.480 --> 11:43.700
<i>We apologize for the inconvenience caused.</i>

11:43.700 --> 11:44.350
Yuki.

11:44.800 --> 11:45.780
Seriously?

11:45.070 --> 11:46.140
What? That sucks!

11:45.780 --> 11:47.810
How long's this gonna take?

11:48.230 --> 11:50.800
<i>Yuki couldn't hear the announcement.</i>

11:50.800 --> 11:54.060
<i>She looked lost because 
she didn't know what was going on.</i>

11:54.480 --> 11:58.250
<i>Part of it was because I couldn't 
walk over to her in that packed train,</i>

11:58.250 --> 12:03.690
<i>but I mainly felt terrible I couldn't 
use sign to tell her anything.</i>

12:04.950 --> 12:09.490
<i>That was what led me to start 
studying sign language for real.</i>

12:11.900 --> 12:17.340
<i>I probably wanted to make the world 
a better place for her in my own way.</i>

12:18.530 --> 12:22.020
<i>I just wish I could've been 
more upfront about it.</i>

12:23.860 --> 12:27.220
Yuki, do you think something's 
off with me today?

12:27.900 --> 12:33.350
<i>Not "off," but you're not your usual self.</i>

12:34.990 --> 12:40.040
I'm just trying not to be 
so prickly all the time.

12:40.040 --> 12:43.180
<i>Huh? Why isn't he signing?</i>

12:44.610 --> 12:47.770
<i>Did you get into a fight with someone?</i>

12:47.770 --> 12:48.730
Like who?

12:49.790 --> 12:53.690
Well, I guess you could call it a "fight"...

13:01.570 --> 13:05.100
<i>When I started college...</i>

13:07.230 --> 13:13.350
<i>I was surrounded by strangers, who 
obviously knew nothing about my disability.</i>

13:13.430 --> 13:15.850
<b>American Football Club
Recruiting new members!!
Players and support staff welcome</b>

13:13.430 --> 13:15.850
<b>American Football Club
Recruiting new members!!
Players and support staff welcome</b>

13:24.490 --> 13:27.240
<b></b>Are you gonna join a club?

13:24.490 --> 13:27.240
<b></b>Are you gonna join a club?

13:28.630 --> 13:29.400
<i>But...</i>

13:29.700 --> 13:33.230
<i>Every time you talked to me in sign,</i>

13:30.450 --> 13:32.950
<b></b>I'm thinking about it.

13:30.450 --> 13:32.950
<b></b>I'm thinking about it.

13:33.230 --> 13:35.330
<i>it gave me a huge lift.</i>

13:36.530 --> 13:38.290
<i>It helped me keep going.</i>

13:40.740 --> 13:46.490
<i>I'm sure there are people around you who 
understand how nice you can be, deep down.</i>

13:47.540 --> 13:48.460
<i>So...</i>

13:49.550 --> 13:52.590
<i>Don't fret over it. Just be a bit more sincere.</i>

13:53.010 --> 13:54.720
That's your conclusion?!

14:01.010 --> 14:02.100
Well, I'll take it.

14:04.860 --> 14:05.820
Roger that.

14:09.860 --> 14:11.900
<i>After all these years, it just hit me.</i>

14:12.740 --> 14:17.240
<i>How much do I really know about Oushi-kun?</i>

14:18.310 --> 14:23.860
<i>I don't know if he'll take 
what I just said to heart...</i>

14:25.140 --> 14:28.520
<i>but I hope he cheers up soon.</i>

14:36.490 --> 14:37.520
Hello?

14:37.980 --> 14:40.620
<i>Emma, is now a good time?</i>

14:40.620 --> 14:45.110
Yeah, I just got off work. What's up?

14:45.540 --> 14:46.910
Do you have time this weekend?

14:48.280 --> 14:50.610
Yeah. Anywhere you wanna go.

14:51.100 --> 14:52.770
<i>But somewhere quiet where we can talk.</i>

14:53.320 --> 14:56.450
Huh? What're we talking about this time?

14:57.550 --> 14:58.830
<i>I'll tell you when we meet.</i>

15:01.750 --> 15:06.420
Oh, okay. I'll let you know 
when I think of something.

15:06.420 --> 15:09.530
<i>Thanks. Later.</i>

15:09.530 --> 15:10.250
Yeah...

15:12.710 --> 15:14.090
Shin-chan?

15:14.720 --> 15:17.470
<b>Yummy Coffee and Snacks</b>

15:15.310 --> 15:17.470
Welcome on board.

15:17.860 --> 15:22.730
First, memorize where the cutlery 
and cookware are stored.

15:23.040 --> 15:25.720
These burr mills are for grinding coffee beans.

15:26.170 --> 15:28.490
We hand-drip our coffee.

15:28.890 --> 15:33.450
When a customer walks in, prep the water 
glasses and wet towels here, okay?

15:36.250 --> 15:36.990
Okay.

15:37.320 --> 15:39.100
Let's give it a shot.

15:40.910 --> 15:42.250
Welcome!

15:52.460 --> 15:54.140
Here's your staff meal.

15:54.450 --> 15:57.770
Do you mind if I ask what you're 
going to use your pay on?

15:58.140 --> 16:00.100
<b></b>I want to pay off my phone first,

15:58.140 --> 16:00.100
<b></b>I want to pay off my phone first,

16:00.390 --> 16:03.650
<b></b>and then save up for traveling.

16:00.390 --> 16:03.650
<b></b>and then save up for traveling.

16:03.880 --> 16:05.400
Traveling, huh?

16:05.710 --> 16:06.860
With friends?

16:10.770 --> 16:12.930
I see how it is now!

16:12.930 --> 16:14.540
Better put in the work, then!

16:16.250 --> 16:20.260
Okay, eat up and get ready 
for the afternoon shift!

16:27.420 --> 16:29.420
Today

16:27.420 --> 16:29.420
I'm here.

16:34.510 --> 16:35.690
Shin-chan.

16:36.510 --> 16:38.130
Sorry, did you wait long?

16:38.530 --> 16:41.420
I got us your favorite caffè mochas.

16:44.790 --> 16:47.310
This place is really pretty at night.

16:47.980 --> 16:50.100
I thought it'd be much darker here.

16:50.750 --> 16:52.170
Well, the moon's out.

16:52.920 --> 17:00.120
I chose here 'cause I heard there're fancy 
cafés and food trucks during the day.

17:00.120 --> 17:00.580
Emma.

17:02.270 --> 17:03.170
Take a seat.

17:04.710 --> 17:05.560
Okay.

17:10.100 --> 17:14.300
Shin-chan, you haven't been 
drinking at all lately, have you?

17:20.060 --> 17:21.560
Did something happen?

17:24.170 --> 17:27.000
Itsu-kun has a girlfriend.

17:35.060 --> 17:36.520
Oh.

17:37.580 --> 17:42.030
Sorry. I guess I put an 
extra load on your mind.

17:44.020 --> 17:45.110
You've got me.

17:46.420 --> 17:47.880
I'm not saying this to console you.

17:48.430 --> 17:51.030
If anything, it's what I want.

17:53.410 --> 17:54.630
Just pick me.

17:55.570 --> 17:58.080
What are you even saying?

17:58.080 --> 17:59.110
I'm being serious.

18:00.890 --> 18:01.720
Listen.

18:02.490 --> 18:05.340
We've known each other 
for years and years now.

18:05.730 --> 18:08.650
Yes, there were times when I thought 
that maybe you were into me.

18:09.110 --> 18:10.990
But do you remember?

18:11.520 --> 18:16.900
When your girlfriend said she knew you 
were in love with me anyway, you replied...

18:17.610 --> 18:21.010
Emma's the one person 
I will never fall for, even if it kills me.

18:22.730 --> 18:25.750
Well, I was planning on taking it to my grave.

18:30.930 --> 18:32.120
Huh?!

18:36.170 --> 18:37.990
<i>Goodnight, guys.</i>

18:39.940 --> 18:43.180
<i>I wonder if Itsuomi-san's still working.</i>

18:43.810 --> 18:45.900
<i>I haven't gotten to see him lately.</i>

18:49.270 --> 18:52.440
You asleep?

18:50.530 --> 18:52.440
<i>Oh, Itsuomi-san!</i>

18:54.520 --> 18:58.440
I'm awake.

18:56.690 --> 18:58.440
Gimme a bit.

18:57.820 --> 18:58.440
<i>Hmm?</i>

19:01.580 --> 19:04.050
<i>Not a peep since.</i>

19:04.700 --> 19:10.710
You asleep?

19:04.700 --> 19:10.710
I'm awake.

19:04.700 --> 19:10.710
Gimme a bit.

19:04.700 --> 19:10.710
Sure.

19:05.170 --> 19:06.650
<i>Itsuomi-san?</i>

19:07.370 --> 19:10.710
Outside.

19:09.570 --> 19:10.710
<i>"Outside"?</i>

19:14.610 --> 19:16.630
<i>Huh? Why?!</i>

19:17.550 --> 19:19.300
<b></b>You look surprised.

19:17.550 --> 19:19.300
<b></b>You look surprised.

19:19.800 --> 19:22.550
<b></b>What are you doing here?

19:19.800 --> 19:22.550
<b></b>What are you doing here?

19:23.470 --> 19:25.450
<i>Maybe he can't see 
because of the light behind me.</i>

19:26.290 --> 19:27.560
<i>I'll come downstairs!</i>

19:28.060 --> 19:31.190
<b></b>Nah, I'm gonna head out.

19:28.060 --> 19:31.190
<b></b>Nah, I'm gonna head out.

19:30.600 --> 19:32.490
<i>Huh? He's leaving?</i>

19:33.060 --> 19:35.440
<i>I couldn't read the signs too well in the dark.</i>

19:36.220 --> 19:40.210
<i>The night is blocking the things 
I want to say to him.</i>

19:58.020 --> 19:59.070
You okay there?

20:02.970 --> 20:06.180
<i>I was just so happy I got to see you!</i>

20:06.570 --> 20:09.630
Yeah, we haven't met for a few days.

20:11.670 --> 20:14.290
Well, you're dressed light.

20:14.730 --> 20:16.440
<i>Wait, I'm in PJs!</i>

20:27.820 --> 20:29.500
Were you about to go to sleep?

20:31.550 --> 20:33.000
I was just in the nick of time, huh?

20:33.860 --> 20:37.750
Sign language is good for 
communicating over distances,

20:38.110 --> 20:40.790
but it's hard without good lighting, huh?

20:41.770 --> 20:43.150
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

20:44.170 --> 20:48.350
<i>When he holds me tight, 
I can feel the vibrations when he talks.</i>

20:49.010 --> 20:53.750
<i>It's melting away my frustration from before.</i>

20:57.020 --> 20:59.270
How was your first day at work?

20:59.970 --> 21:02.690
<i>I was nervous, but the day 
flew by in an instant.</i>

21:03.290 --> 21:04.220
Great.

21:05.160 --> 21:09.750
<i>Meetings like these are going 
to get rarer as we go.</i>

21:11.190 --> 21:14.540
<i>I'll do my best to cut costs 
and save money for a while.</i>

21:16.360 --> 21:19.290
Just don't stretch it too thin. 
Including your time.

21:20.510 --> 21:24.550
There are plenty of things 
out there to do for free.

21:24.970 --> 21:29.430
We can line up our schedules and go on dates 
for half a day, or even just a few hours.

21:30.280 --> 21:35.310
We haven't made plans and gone anywhere 
since we started dating, huh?

21:35.930 --> 21:38.440
On that note, where would you like to go?

21:40.390 --> 21:42.430
<i>Are you sure I can pick?</i>

21:44.770 --> 21:50.440
<i>I was so focused on saving money and 
traveling overseas that I didn't realize.</i>

21:50.950 --> 21:54.250
<i>Of course it's okay to plan other things, too.</i>

21:55.310 --> 21:59.620
<i>I get to choose where to go 
on my first date with Itsuomi-san...</i>

21:59.620 --> 22:03.180
Man, I'm really looking forward to it.

22:03.790 --> 22:04.980
<i>Oh, boy.</i>

22:05.590 --> 22:08.770
<i>Where should we go?</i>

22:07.010 --> 22:10.010
Promise

23:15.030 --> 23:30.260
Our World
